//! twin-core: the rules the twin runs every scan, in whole micrometres, millidegrees and milli-newton-metres, with no
//! floating point, no heap, no threads and no I/O, so Kani can prove them for every input (`cargo kani`).
//!
//! - `joint`: an M12 joint from its two halves' element data (generated by `python lib/build.py core`): which poles are made,
//!   marginal, open, high-resistance or blocked at any gap, key error, torque and contact condition. A port of
//!   lib/toolkit/contact.py `mate()`; the golden tests hold the two to the same answers.
//! - `safety`: the motor-starter cell's emergency-stop channel: dual-channel input, manual reset, K1 feedback.
//! - `generated`: the halves, the joints and the golden cases, from the elements as built.
//! - `proofs` (only under Kani): the properties, for every input within the stated bounds.
pub mod units;
pub mod joint;
pub mod safety;
pub mod generated;
#[cfg(kani)]
mod proofs;
